When patch 2 first came out I wrote a note here asking for help
on dealing with a compiler bug characterized by the message

cc -O -I../include -c dogmove.c
compiler error: schain botch

I simply unpacked the source code from scratch again & it compiled.

When I got the same error in vault.c with patch 3 I decided to try
something easier, and it worked.

Being a mediocre C programmer my first try was certain to be full of
deep meaning:  I added a one variable declaration of the form

int dummy;

A bolt of lightning then struck the terminal and a voice boomed out:

"You have discovered the secret of cc, Mortal!"


Laugh if you want, but it worked!


